===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# To provide a [[service]] to (someone); to act as a [[servant]] to (someone); to serve (someone) as a [[waiter]] or [[waitress]] in a restaurant.
#: {{syn|en|attend to|Thesaurus:serve}}
#: {{ux|en|Is someone '''waiting on''' you yet?}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merry Wives|I|1|text=How now, Simple! where have you been? I must '''wait on''' myself, must I?}}
#* {{RQ:Charlotte Bronte Jane Eyre|II|I|page=6|text={{...}} for such a large house there are very few servants, because master has never lived here much; and when he does come, being a bachelor, he needs little '''waiting on''':}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1942|author=w:Zora Neale Hurston|title=w:Dust Tracks on a Road|location=New York|publisher=Arno Press|year_published=1969|chapter=9|page=171|url=https://archive.org/details/dusttracksonroad00hurs/page/171
